# CANOPY screens — what this deployment shows where

This guide was built from the deployment's screen library, so it lists exactly
the screens CANOPY serves here. It answers *which* screen; the canopy-operator
skill says how to open it.

## Finding a screen

1. Look the device up by its system and label, the name operators use
   ("SR: BPM 37", "SR: ION-PUMP 38", "SR: EPU7"). A numbered run is written
   first–last: "ION-PUMP 37–42" holds ION-PUMP 38.
2. Prefer the main screen that shows it. A screen whose name starts with `_`
   is a detail its parent opens; open it directly when the detail is what was
   asked for.
3. Open it with `set_workspace` and `{"cmd": "open", "args": {"ref": "<ref>"}}`.
4. A device not listed here is on no screen: find its channels with the
   channel finder and plot them in the Data Browser instead.
